module controls

// What a walker's player asks of it each tick, apart from the game so that
// the game and a client's sample program (sample.kest) share the one type.

// What a player asks for, each -1 to 1: to run along x and z, and to jump
// (above a half); and where it has turned its view, radians about +Y as a
// camera's yaw, within half a turn either way. With a
// headset's controller, where its right hand holds the walker's
// lamp: meters from where the head was as the headset began, turned with
// the view, and `holding` above a half while the hand is located.
struct Stick {
    runX: f32
    runZ: f32
    jump: f32
    heading: f32
    handX: f32
    handY: f32
    handZ: f32
    holding: f32
}
